        <abstract>
            <para>The data contain 410 occurrences of amphibians and reptiles recorded during time-constrained encounter surveys in six rainforest remnants of the Valparai Plateau, Anamalai Hills, Tamil Nadu, India, between September and October 2017. Twenty-five incidental records of mammals and herpetofauna have also been included.</para><para>The data from time-constrained encounter surveys correspond to the following publication: </para><para>Harikrishnan, S., Mudappa, D. &amp; Raman, T. R. S. 2018. Herpetofaunal survey in rainforest remnants of the Anamalai Hills in the Western Ghats, India. The Herpetological Bulletin 146: 8-17. URL: https://www.thebhs.org/publications/the-herpetological-bulletin/issue-number-146-winter-2018/1870-02-herpetofaunal-survey-in-rainforest-remnants-of-the-western-ghats-india/file</para>
        </abstract>
